            {
               "text": "### Images from Tohoku\n\nThese images are copyright for Tohoku and allowed to be used according to the license determined by them.\n\nTo visualize all images, use the left and right arrows on the slide below.",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p><div class=\"htSlides\"><div class=\"htSlide\"><div class=\"htSlideCounter\">1 / 2</div><img class=\"imgGameSize\" id=\"imgTohoku\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('imgTohoku', '0%')\"><div class=\"htSlideCaption\">Kon'yo bankoku zenzu. Mantido por Tohoku University Main Library (<htcite0>).</div><div class=\"htSlideRefs\"><b>Related content:</b><ul><li>Where is the center? - We explain the different centers of the planet from the perspective of different peoples. (<htcite2>)</li><li>Chronology - Is it possible to create a universal timeline applicable to all of humanity? (<htcite3>)</li></ul></div></div><div class=\"htSlide\"><div class=\"htSlideCounter\">2 / 2</div><img class=\"imgGameSize\" id=\"imgSoroban\" onclick=\"htImageZoom('imgSoroban', '0%')\"><div class=\"htSlideCaption\">Soroban (算盤) by Shigetoshi Oyabu. Maintained by Tohoku University Main Library (<htcite1>).</div><div class=\"htSlideRefs\"><b>Related content:</b><ul><li>Higher orders with Soroban and Suanpan (算盤): In this text, we learn how to represent orders higher than the units in the different versions of the abacus  (<htcite4>).</li><li>Adding with Soroban, Suanpan (算盤) and Schyoty (счёты): In this text, we learn to add numbers from 0 to 9 using tools developed in Asia (<htcite5>).</li><li>Building to count (Soroban, 算盤): In this text, we explore how we can count using a Japanese instrument (<htcite6>).</li></ul></div></div><i class=\"fa-solid fa-chevron-left htSlidePrev\" onclick=\"htPlusDivs(-1);\"></i><i class=\"fa-solid fa-chevron-right htSlideNext\" onclick=\"htPlusDivs(1);\"></i></div></p>",
